Skip Reanimated synchronous Android prop updates for view tags that are no longer mounted.
On React Native 0.86 Reanimated 4.5.1 calls MountingManager.updatePropsSynchronously by reflection; for an unmounted tag it throws and the full stack trace is logged on the UI thread
(about 2,400 warnings in 30 s of normal navigation on a Pixel 8; upstream reports an ANR cluster from it: https://github.com/software-mansion/react-native-reanimated/issues/10280).
Same change as upstream https://github.com/software-mansion/react-native-reanimated/pull/10435, released in 4.7.1.
Not bumped yet: 4.6/4.7 bring many other changes, and the RN 0.86 bump PR stays as small as possible.
Remove when react-native-reanimated is bumped to >=4.7.1 (LIVE-41251).

diff --git a/android/src/main/java/com/swmansion/reanimated/NativeProxy.kt b/android/src/main/java/com/swmansion/reanimated/NativeProxy.kt
index 48e37714232d5ccf74d99d61cb2fac56314087aa..450cd8e644835ed0e537ddad665e7a5a402195af 100644
--- a/android/src/main/java/com/swmansion/reanimated/NativeProxy.kt
+++ b/android/src/main/java/com/swmansion/reanimated/NativeProxy.kt
@@ -245,6 +245,11 @@ open class NativeProxy {
